Interrupt remapping (remapping.rs, D594) was written by the EggOS project from these sources,
read to learn how the hardware works; no code was copied or translated:

- Intel Virtualization Technology for Directed I/O, Architecture Specification (chapters 5, 6,
  9 and 10: the DMAR table, interrupt remapping entries, the invalidation queue).
- AMD I/O Virtualization Technology (IOMMU) Specification (chapters 2 and 3: the IVRS table,
  device table entries, the 128-bit interrupt remapping entry, the command buffer).
- IA-PC HPET (High Precision Event Timers) Specification 1.0a.
